  "blocker": "Foot-tarsal Kabsch residuals are teaching-grade (mean \u22482.3 mm, max \u22484.3 mm talus \u2014 comparable to UM\u2192BP3D), but VHM gastrocnemius med/lat bellies land entirely at X>0 (wrong_side vs BP3D right-foot convention X\u22640). Soleus is only partially inside a 40 mm-padded foot AABB (frac \u226a 0.85) with centroid X>0. Root cause: 7 co-located tarsal landmarks (~50 mm span) leave long-axis angular freedom; calf bellies ~250\u2013350 mm proximal amplify small rotation error into large lateral offset (leverage). Trial adding synthetic BP3D distal tibia/fibula landmarks improved laterality but blew foot residuals (mean \u22488.3 mm, max \u224817.8 mm) \u2014 unacceptable. No BP3D tibia/fibula meshes exist in this right-foot pack for a proper LE Kabsch. Do NOT wire main-tree until proximal shared landmarks or an alternate registration is available.",
